# Tapestry XSS: <span jwcid="@Insert" ... raw="true" /> disables Tapestry's
# default HTML output escaping. Any value bound to that Insert is written to the
# page verbatim. If the value is user- or tenant-influenced (help text, FAQ
# answers, news items, welcome text, contact info, notes) this is a stored-XSS
# sink (CWE-79).
#
# Complements KEUR-XSS-001 (Angular bypassSecurityTrust*). Apache Tapestry 4.x
# escapes @Insert output by default; raw="true" opts out of that escaping, so a
# single attribute turns a safe render into an injection point.
#
# Match @Insert components that carry raw="true". The data source cannot be
# judged statically, so this is a warn (needs human triage: is the bound value
# user-influenced?).
id: KEUR-XSS-002
ilities: [integrity]
maturity: 1
title: Tapestry XSS — @Insert raw="true" disables output escaping
category: xss
severity: warning
engine: pattern
action: warn
target:
  extensions: .html .jwc .script
  exclude_paths: /test/ /tests/ node_modules/
patterns:
  - regex: jwcid\s*=\s*"[^"]*@Insert[^"]*"[^>]*\braw\s*=\s*"true"
    message: Tapestry @Insert with raw="true" writes the bound value to the page without HTML-escaping (CWE-79). If the value is user- or tenant-influenced this is a stored-XSS sink. Confirm the source is fully trusted, or drop raw="true" so Tapestry escapes it.
confidence: 0.55
fix: Remove raw="true" so Tapestry HTML-escapes the output. Only keep it for values that are provably trusted (constant markup you control). For user-supplied rich text, sanitise server-side (e.g. OWASP Java HTML Sanitizer) before rendering.
